    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The controller of your data is [RELLENAR: nombre y dos apellidos], with
      Spanish tax ID (NIF) [RELLENAR: NIF], with address at
      [RELLENAR: dirección], who operates PreFrame ("we") — see the
      <a href="/legal/aviso-legal/">Legal Notice</a>. You can reach us at the
      address in section 10.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What data is processed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account data.</strong> When you sign in with Google or Apple
        we receive your email address, your name and, with Google, your avatar.
        We never receive or store a password.</li>
      <li><strong>Your projects.</strong> The shots, sections, notes and
        equipment you create are stored in your account so you can open them on
        your computer. The audio and image files you work with stay on your
        machine and are never uploaded (section 5).</li>
      <li><strong>Usage data.</strong> Product events such as "project created"
        or "export completed", tied to your account id, used to understand how
        the application is used. They never include the content of your
        projects.</li>
      <li><strong>Error reports.</strong> See section 4.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment data.</strong> Payments are processed by Stripe as
        merchant of record. PreFrame never sees your card number; we only
        receive confirmation that a purchase was completed and which credits to
        deliver, and keep a record of your purchases so you can see them in the
        application.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Providing the service</strong> — account, projects, credits
        and purchases: necessary to perform the contract with you
        (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li>
      <li><strong>Understanding how the application is used and fixing what
        breaks</strong> — usage events and error reports: our legitimate
        interest in improving PreFrame (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object at
        any time (section 9).</li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligations</strong> — tax and accounting records of
        purchases, kept by Stripe and by us as the law requires
        (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your data and do not use it for advertising.</p>

    <!-- Sistema de error reports aún no en producción: el compromiso se
         publica desde el día uno. El interruptor en Ajustes sí existe. -->
    <h2>4. Error reports</h2>
    <p>
      When something breaks inside the application, PreFrame can send us a
      technical report so we can find out and fix it. The report contains
      the error message, a sanitised stack trace, the PreFrame version, your
      operating system and your account id. It <strong>never</strong> contains
      the content of your projects, nor the names or paths of your files.
    </p>
    <p>
      We process these reports on the basis of our legitimate interest in
      keeping the application working (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). They are deleted
      automatically after <strong>90 days</strong>. Sending them is on by
      default and you can turn it off at any time in
      <strong>Settings → Error reports</strong>; from that moment nothing is
      sent.
    </p>

    <!-- "The files you work with", y no la lista de qué tipos de archivo son:
         para el compromiso de privacidad basta con decir DÓNDE están, y el
         detalle describía el funcionamiento de la app (misma decisión que en
         el apartado 4 de los Términos). -->
    <h2>5. Where your data lives</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your computer.</strong> Your projects are cached locally, and
        the files you work with (audio and reference images) exist only on your
        machine. PreFrame never uploads them.</li>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> (Supabase, Inc.), which hosts our database
        and authentication in the European Union (AWS, <strong>eu-west-1</strong>,
        Ireland). Account data, projects, usage events and error reports are
        stored there.</li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong> (Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd.), which
        processes payments as merchant of record under its own
        <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> and <strong>Apple</strong>, only as sign-in
        providers: when you sign in they tell us who you are; we do not share
        anything with them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. This website</h2>
    <p>
      The PreFrame website (preframe-app.com) is hosted on
      <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, a service of GitHub, Inc. (United States).
      Like any web server, GitHub keeps technical logs of the requests it
      receives, including the visitor's IP address, in order to deliver and
      secure the service. That processing is GitHub's own and is governed by
      their privacy policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site uses <strong>no cookies and no browser storage</strong>, which
      is why you are never asked to accept anything. Every font is served from
      this same domain: no requests are made to Google Fonts or to advertising
      networks. The only request to a third party is the cookieless analytics
      script described in section 7.
    </p>

    <!-- Conectado el 2026-08-07: Cloudflare Web Analytics. Si algún día se
         añade un proveedor con eventos (Umami/Plausible) para medir el clic de
         descarga, hay que ampliar esta sección: hoy dice expresamente que los
